{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>וְאִם הַעְלֵם יַעְלִימוּ</b> — The reason for the doubling is to say that if they concealed the matter from the first one, they are no longer able to avoid concealing it from those who come after him, and they will surely conceal it from all of them — for if they wish to bring them to justice they will say to them, ״Why did you not bring the first one to justice?״ Or it may mean <b>הַעְלֵם</b> — that they did not prevent him from giving to Molech; <b>יַעְלִימוּ</b> — that they refrained from executing judgment upon him after he had given, as the verse says, ״בְּתִתּוֹ מִזַּרְעוֹ״ and so forth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:49.057993756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}